# mcp/jev — jev (TypeSafe System One decision model) MCP server.
# Pure stdlib MCP (no pip deps).
#
# Two providers, identical request/answer shape. Auto-selected:
#   * TYPESAFE_API_KEY set -> TypeSafe direct
#       POST https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone
#       Authorization: Bearer $TYPESAFE_API_KEY
#       model: jev-latest (also jev-1.13.0 / jev-1.14.0)
#       No free tier, no public bearer, no paid-fallback retry.
#   * otherwise            -> OpenCode zen relay (default)
#       model jev-1.13-free (free tier) / jev-1.13 (paid) at
#       https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/systemone with the OpenCode desktop fingerprint
#       (UA opencode/1.18.31 + x-opencode-client: desktop + x-opencode-project:
#       global). Auth: real OPENCODE_ZEN_API_KEY -> Bearer <key>; no key ->
#       Bearer public (relay free tier, verified HTTP 200 for jev-1.13-free);
#       anonymous -> 403 FreeTierError. Non-free models require a real key.
#       On free-tier exhaustion (HTTP 429/403) WITH a real key, retries paid
#       jev-1.13 (JEV_FALLBACK_TO_PAID / JEV_FALLBACK_MODEL) on the same
#       key/endpoint/UA. JEV_FALLBACK_TO_PAID=0 fails open. No-key never falls
#       back (no key => no paid route). No fallback to NON-JEV models.
# JEV_PROVIDER=opencode forces the relay even when TYPESAFE_API_KEY is present.
#
# Keys are NOT set here: mcp-jev reads them from the active profile's local .env
# (never committed) because Hermes does not inject profile secrets into MCP
# subprocesses. Reference: https://github.com/ronail/jev-cost-guard/blob/main/mcp/jev/env.example
# optional — the server defaults these; uncomment only to override
# JEV_PROVIDER=typesafe        # typesafe | opencode (auto-detected otherwise)
# JEV_MODEL=jev-1.13-free      # typesafe default: jev-latest
# JEV_ENDPOINT=https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/systemone   # typesafe: https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone
# JEV_FALLBACK_TO_PAID=1        # opencode only; default 1; 0 = fail-open (no paid retry)
# JEV_FALLBACK_MODEL=jev-1.13  # opencode only; paid model on free-tier exhaustion
# JEV_FIND_MAX_CALLS=12        # jev_find: jev calls per invocation (hard cap 40)
JEV_MCP=1          # on (default); set 0 to disable trimmer behaviour
JEV_DEBUG=0        # emit [jev-debug] POST/resp traces to stderr
